  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-gitview",
      "text": "A Git panel for the [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) Web sidebar."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-gitview",
      "text": "- Working-tree changes, staging and commits\n- Unified or side-by-side diffs with syntax highlighting\n- Commit graph, branches, blame and reflog\n- CI status for GitHub, GitLab and Gitea; step details for GitHub Actions\n- Optional commit-message generation using the session's selected model\n- A wide **Git** tab beside Chat and Trajectory, with a Review mode (stage, commit, side-by-side diff) and a Repository mode (history, branches, CI)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Requires Node.js **24+**, Git, pnpm, and one of the DSH versions listed under `engines.dsh` in `package.json` (each one is install-tested in CI). Other DSH versions are not tested; [rdsh](https://github.com/jimoto-no-llm/rustdsh) installs this plugin by default and moves DSH along its `rc` channel, so new tags are checked weekly against that list. Desktop is not tested.\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-gitview\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Restart DSH with your existing options and port, then open **Git** in the right sidebar or as a tab beside Chat and Trajectory. Do not enable an older manually installed Git panel alongside this package.\n\nTo remove:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web remove dsh-gitview\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Placement",
      "text": "Settings → General → **Git view placement** chooses the right sidebar, the conversation tab, or both (default). The choice is stored per browser, not per user or session."
    },
    {
      "section": "CI and AI",
      "text": "GitHub uses the host's `gh` authentication. GitLab and Gitea use `GITLAB_TOKEN` and `GITEA_TOKEN`; without credentials, public CI is attempted. Self-hosted services require an explicit provider and token-environment-variable mapping in the plugin configuration.\n\nCI is polled while the panel is visible and focused. Checks left pending for over 24 hours are marked as overdue, not successful. This plugin does not rerun or cancel CI."
    },
    {
      "section": "CI and AI",
      "text": "Commit-message generation sends **staged changes** to the selected model provider and may incur charges. It does not commit automatically. **Ask AI** adds CI metadata to your chat draft without sending it; logs are not attached. Authentication tokens are not returned to the browser."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "The browser half is written in `src/client/` and built into `lib/client.js`, which is committed because the Host serves it verbatim:\n\n```sh\nnpm ci\nnpm run build   # src/client → lib/client.js\nnpm run check   # types, a stale-build check, syntax\nnpm test\n\nTests need `js-yaml@4.3.2` available through `NODE_PATH`. Package verification also needs pnpm and a DSH listed in `engines.dsh` (`DSH_BIN` selects the binary):\n\n```sh\nnpm run test:package\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "This builds a `.tgz`, checks its contents, and tests standard installation, configuration composition and removal in a temporary DSH profile. It does not start a server or call a model. The verified package is saved in `dist/`. GitHub Actions runs these checks once per listed DSH version and retains the package artifacts for 14 days. After a push to `main` passes every listed version, CI publishes the `package.json` version to npm through trusted publishing and creates its `v<version>` release, unless npm already has that version."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "To see whether npm has published a DSH version the list does not cover yet:\n\n```sh\nnpm run test:track\n```\n\nThe same check runs weekly in GitHub Actions. To add a version: install it, run `DSH_BIN=<path> npm run test:package`, then add the version to `engines.dsh` and both `peerDependencies` in `package.json`."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "[MIT](LICENSE)"
    }
  ],
